WEBVTT

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.150
Now that Ippo-kun has finally healed up,

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:13.060
we're all going to get together and celebrate his victory over Sawamura.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.280
Yeah!

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.000
I've never fished off a boat before!

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.660
Me neither. Maybe I'll catch some tuna.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.860
I'll help if you manage to hook a whale!

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.170
A whale? Damn!

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.790
I'd say they're setting the bar high.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.800
Let's stop here. This is a good place to fish.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.660
What the hell? We aren't that far out to sea!

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.210
You think we can catch any whales here?

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.310
They'd just sink our boat.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.390
You kidding me? That sucks.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:49.540
You're able to catch goby, sillago, flounder, flathead, and rockfish around here.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.900
Am I right?

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.210
You really know your fishing, Yagi-san!

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.910
Now, I didn't come here just to sit around with a pole in hand.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.650
Why don't we spice things up with a contest?

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.460
We'll pair up and see who catches the most fish.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.910
The pair that finishes last goes to bed hungry.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:07.770
Sounds great!

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.290
I like what I'm hearing.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.610
Count me in!

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.420
Me too!

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.280
Now then, time to draw straws.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.550
Count me out, I have stuff to do around here.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.470
And I'm on the clock.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.310
So that means...

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.040
these three teams will battle it out.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.040
{OP}

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.730
First, you'll need to lower the 
lines all the way to the bottom.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:39.110
If you're not getting anything, jerk the pole two or three times, then lower the line again.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.830
Oh, look who's the fisherman.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.240
I've gotten really used to this job.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.800
Are we really gonna catch anything?

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.810
They'll start biting soon.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.000
Oh yeah!

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.320
I guess there are fish out here.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.380
Only a matter of time before we catch something.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.590
Got one!

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.920
Ooh! Now that's a big one!

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.220
Why won't they come to us?

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.660
{ \an8}That's a great catch! I'm impressed!

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.660
If you wait, they will come.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.100
Fishing requires patience!

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.470
Yeah!

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:09.890
Hmph!

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.790
They're on a roll!

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.570
Concentrate, Takamura!

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.850
Got one!

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.860
I got two!

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.130
Kid?

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:21.780
Yes, sir?

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.910
Can we move to a different spot? We're not having any luck here.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.990
O-Okay, we're moving out.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.920
This is also a good spot.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.880
And what a spot it is!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.510
I can see why!

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.740
What is this?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.340
Quit reeling in the strange ones!

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:50.410
A double hit!

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.830
Looking at Yagi-chan and Shinoda-kun gives me the crazy feeling...

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:58.270
{overlap}They look nice and big! We rock!

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.290
...that they're super-experienced fishermen!

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:01.470
They didn't rent those rods either! They're completely customized!

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.840
They're competing knowing that they'll win?!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.490
{overlap}Aw! Another double hit!

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.490
I thought something was up when he brought out those sticks.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.690
You gotta catch some, old man, or else we're not eating!

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.790
You need to do something, too!

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.440
Wow, nicely caught, Master Shinoda.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.320
Heaven forefend! This humble soul will never be a Yagi-dono.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.090
You hear what they're saying?

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:28.300
I don't recognize this Yagi-chan!

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.510
Still, we can't be on the same boat and not catch anything.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.140
They must have longer poles.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.400
"Longer poles"?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.720
How positively quaint.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.860
Let it go. They are rank amateurs.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.590
This is pretty easy!

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:52.910
We're catching a lot.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.830
<i>Those assholes.</i>

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>How could those two have any talent besides boxing?</i>

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.540
I finally got one!

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.610
Yes! You did it, Takamura!

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.090
Look at this, you clowns!

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.850
It got away!

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.850
That's a shame, Takamura-dono!

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.730
What did you do, you numbskull!

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.290
You catch any fish, dumbass?

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.860
Jump in and snag the damn fish!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.870
Y-You just call me a dumbass?

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.420
They're now out for blood.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.740
You don't like it, then knock me out, why dontcha?

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.610
I knew this would happen.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:34.530
I'm gonna catch something so big, you'll be shitting your pants!

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.540
Whales! Come to Daddy!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:39.910
Watch it!

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.390
Don't rock the boat, stupid!

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.530
Takamura-san, you need to calm down!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.300
Shut up! Shut up!

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.860
This is dangerous!

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.880
Guys, grab hold of something!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.800
Please stop, Takamura-san!

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.770
C'mere! C'mere!

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:56.810
What the...

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.560
I really got one!

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.270
I'm a damn natural!

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.640
It's big! Be careful!

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:04.900
It ain't getting away!

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:06.330
It's coming up!

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.530
Look at those stripes!

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.590
I'm gonna land you now!

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.330
Wh-What the hell was that?

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.800
It looked like Aoki.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.000
You boob! You sent him overboard!

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.550
Aoki-san!

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.260
And that's how it happened.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.040
I guess we can't laugh it off.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.810
I almost died out there, for crying out loud!

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.600
It happened under my watch. I'm ashamed.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.520
And this jackass!

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.660
Pretending to be asleep, are you?!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.630
Didn't get much sleep.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:53.490
I had mosquitoes in my room.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.220
Then smack them out of the air!

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.330
You saying your jab got rusty?!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.660
Say that again?

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:02.380
Easy, guys. At least we're here in one piece.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.160
Coach,

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:06.680
can we change the subject to something serious?

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:07.670
Yes.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.050
All right, men,

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.500
listen carefully.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.180
I got a bit of news for you.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:22.430
The WBC middleweight title match!

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:28.440
Takamura will officially be making a run at his second world title.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.430
Oh?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.750
They took their sweet time!

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:43.670
You call that a bit of news? That's incredible, Coach!

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.810
That's a big deal!

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.830
We're counting on you, Takamura-san!

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:49.190
Sure!

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.950
Winning that title will be easier than fishing you out of the water.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:56.430
I take it back! I hope you get your ass beat!

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.360
Wanna do another catch and release?

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.850
Guys, easy!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.830
Aoki! Kimura!

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.180
You two need to get down to business!

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:05.940
You mean us?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.570
You two got semi-semifinals on the same day.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.130
Hell, yeah!

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:14.140
Let's kick off his title match with a bang!

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:15.140
Yeah!

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.390
Semi-semi?

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.320
Then what's the semifinal?

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.080
The OPBF title match.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:26.830
Miyata Ichirou will be fighting that night.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.750
Miyata-kun?

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:33.710
Since we'll be in a large arena, we wanted some big-name matchups.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.710
Listen!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:38.810
Itagaki, you concentrate on the next round of the rookie tournament!

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.100
Kid, you keep focusing on getting back to full strength!

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.360
That's all!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.820
<i>Will he ever stop conditioning?!</i>

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.070
<i>He's got Ichirou by the balls.</i>

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:01.530
<i>I made the right choice in having him train with Takamura.</i>

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:05.750
<i>He hasn't trained with a better boxer in a long time.</i>

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.500
<i>This will light a fire under his ass.</i>

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:16.550
Do you Kamogawa Gym people... always practice like this?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.390
If I don't hold back on those guys, I'll end up killing them.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.470
We're going full throttle in this training camp!

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.180
Let's go!

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.560
Slow down, you bastard!

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.060
Well, the only one who can keep up with this is that smart aleck Ippo!

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:37.110
You little cheat!

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.010
<i>This is good practicing.</i>

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:48.720
<i>Damn. My entire body is aching.</i>

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.470
<i>Normally, it'd take a day or three for my body to get used to these things.</i>

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.820
So you took up fishing?

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:03.850
Leave me alone!

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:08.590
There's a guy I really need to show up after camp.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.880
Something's biting.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.530
Too bad.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.480
This is harder than I thought.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.040
Who said you can only eat the damn bait!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.660
Maybe fishing isn't for you.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.600
Fine! Then you try!

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:33.880
It's easy.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:42.260
<i>I just need to do my counter when I see the bobber move.</i>

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.290
It looks like you suck at everything except boxing!

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.810
It won't get away again!

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.040
Something's biting!

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:57.860
All right!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:09:59.430
How's that?

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:02.820
Sucks to be you!

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.660
I'm not taking that from you!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.910
You want me to kill you?!

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:15.120
I thought you were going to dodge that!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:18.170
{overlap}People would usually warn a guy first!

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.170
Isn't it too early in the day for this crap?

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.220
A rod? Never took you for a fisherman.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.930
I need to get back at a guy who made a fool out of me.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.550
Are you talking about Yagi?

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:29.810
Yes, him!

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:33.960
Take it from me, do not challenge Yagi to this.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:34.810
What?

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:39.740
He and I joined Kamogawa Gym around the same time.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:45.490
He loves boxing, but unfortunately, he didn't have the talent.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:51.110
After losing several fights in a row, 
he came to me thinking I could help.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.330
<i>Wanna blow off some steam someplace?</i>

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:55.870
<i> Sounds good!</i>

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.880
<i>But I live a simple life.</i>

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.070
<i>We'll go anywhere, just name it.</i>

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.840
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:09.360
I swear his face was a demon mask.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.450
Oh, I know what you're talking about!

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:18.470
Later, Shinoda-kun told me that there's a fishing pond with a "No fishing hooks or Yagis" sign.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.360
"N-No Yagis"?

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:26.360
If he had taken up professional fishing, 
he'd be a legendary world champ, no doubt.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.360
That asshole!

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:32.000
I'll put an end to that legend!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.940
I tried taking him on a number of times in my younger days. But I always came back defeated.{come - came}

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.330
Shut up!

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.340
<i>He took a full blow.</i>

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.710
<i>He never used to let his guard down.</i>

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.770
We sure ran a lot!

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:05.270
This is normal for me!

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.400
This is why your counters are always weak!

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.540
<i>"Weak"?</i>

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:12.610
We're sparring when we get back!

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:16.200
Wait! Who's sparring against who?

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:19.670
Ain't it obvious? You versus me!

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:26.880
This is a good opportunity to learn from him.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:28.780
Any headgear?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:29.880
No need.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.390
<i>I'm not denying his talents.</i>

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:39.640
<i>But can a heavier boxer keep up with the maximum speed of a lighter boxer?</i>

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.860
<i>He's a former world champion, so I don't need to hold back!</i>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.360
<i>Ichirou certainly has the speed.</i>

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.950
<i>So what are you going to do, Takamura?</i>

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:02.210
<i>He's that fast? Impossible!</i>

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.040
<i>No. He's...</i>

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:10.440
<i>I'm not getting into a slugfest in this corner!</i>

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.180
<i>I'm throwing a punch and getting away!</i>

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.010
<i>A counter!</i>

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:20.850
<i>No way! He cleared it with one hand!</i>

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:21.810
Weak.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:27.020
<i>Weak... Weak... Weak!</i>

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.230
So what do you think?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:42.540
I feel bad. And he pulled his punches to avoid killing me.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:47.170
I never thought someone heavier than me would be faster than me.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.310
That guy is a freak.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:52.300
Nope, he's not faster than you.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.550
In fact, you're several times faster than him.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.780
But he really knows how to use all 36 square meters of a ring.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:06.650
His moves cover the shortest amount of distance possible, making him appear faster than he really is.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:10.410
It's a high-level technique. Hope you learned a lesson.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.710
A lesson, huh?

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.030
What's up?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.970
Are my counters really weak?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.190
They are.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:35.480
Don't think I swatted you off because I'm out of your weight class.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.990
All world-class boxers are capable of doing that.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.180
But I put my full weight into it.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.540
Whenever you throw those counters, you leave your body wide open.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.200
Then you become off balance, which diffuses your strength.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.190
But I'll give you credit for giving it all you got.

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:53.570
Off balance?

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:56.740
My punches pack power.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.200
Fine.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.190
Punch me.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:05.210
I'm retempering your rusty blade!

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.460
Come on! Hit me already!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.690
Rusty blade?

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.450
<i>I'm pushing, but he's still not moving!</i>

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:18.720
Right there!

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.510
Tuck in your elbow!

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:22.470
Now push.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.980
There you go! See the difference?

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:31.070
If you raise your left elbow, it pulls your chest muscles.

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:35.990
It makes it easier to punch, but your right hand also goes out to the side, which dissipates your strength.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:40.780
But if you tuck in your left arm, it stretches your back muscles.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.580
Which leads to...

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.670
I see.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.890
It's a straight-line punch that will leave a dent.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:58.200
It's a compact form, but it'll increase your power and control twofold.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:01.690
So I was just wasting strength with my obsession with counters.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.470
One more thing.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:07.520
You need a stable lower body to maintain that form.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.610
You were wobbly from your hips all the way down.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:14.900
You left Kamogawa Gym so you could find your own way to the top.{can - could}

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.050
You were always practicing alone, too.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:22.310
You may have seen a lot of things, 
but it also blinds you to a lot more.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:27.530
Don't take pride in the fact that you
 train more than lower-ranked boxers.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:29.670
Where do you want to go?

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.690
What are you aiming for?

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:36.940
You won't survive long on the global stage just by giving it all you got.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.950
But you still need to run!

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:41.680
Run, even if you're all by yourself!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:47.020
<i>He knew my weakness? So that's why he made me run that much?</i>

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.850
Did you set up this camp for my sake?

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:52.670
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:56.690
You're such a shitty boxer, I couldn't bear to watch anymore.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:04.200
Even if you did turn your back on us,
 you'll always be one of my dear underlings.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:11.510
<i>I joined Kamogawa Gym before he did, so this domineering attitude is hard to swallow.</i>

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.710
<i>Still...</i>

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:16.850
Anyway, you have my thanks.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.470
I need to thank you.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.680
I'm guessing you know what I know, Pops.

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:33.600
He's going to have some tough fights ahead of him,

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.690
and his counters have gotten rusty.

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:39.330
Yes, I was fully aware of that.

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:43.070
But your helpful advice has changed Ichirou for the better.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.160
For now, he's gotten rid of the rust,

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:50.200
and now his counters are as honed as a Japanese blade.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:53.280
Allow me to ask: Why did you school him?

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:56.240
Counters are the Dempsey Roll's archenemy.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.450
Why would you divulge something that will undercut Makunouchi?

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:01.930
Because it'll be a hoot!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.720
A hoot?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:07.310
If they're gonna fight, I might as well up the entertainment value.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.600
They're both my underlings, you know.

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:16.480
There will be no favorites in that fight. I don't care who wins.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:19.750
But I'm not gonna watch two chumps duke it out.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:23.350
Those two better improve as boxers.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.120
The fight better be as epic as possible!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:28.830
That's the only reason you did that?

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.250
Yeah!

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:34.830
The biggest fight on the biggest stage between the best fighters.

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:37.630
Don't you wanna see that, Pops?

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.590
Guess I do.

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:44.440
Oh, got one.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:48.180
You lucky sonuvabitch!

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:50.690
Takamura-san, welcome back!

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.140
How was camp?

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:56.150
It ain't nothing special. I was just there for basic conditioning.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.090
Right.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:00.690
Yeah, I guess this isn't the right time for any dramatic changes.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.170
What is it?

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.160
<i>Something did change!</i>

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.280
<i>It had to change!</i>

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:09.640
I'll show you the fruits of my training!

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.160
Training?

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.870
You're challenging me? To what?

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:18.670
I heard there's a fishing pond with a "No Yagis" sign.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.880
I'm going to bury you on your home turf!

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:26.670
Well, I'm sure they removed the ban a long time ago.

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:28.880
But we have matches coming up...

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:30.180
Go ahead.

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:33.270
However, that will be your last bit of fun.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.190
Once you're done, you're focusing on that second world title.

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:38.190
Glad to see you're on board.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.400
I know how you feel.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:41.570
Get ‘im.

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.190
Yeah.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.630
Yagi-san, n-now look...

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:48.820
Don't worry. I know he has an important match coming up.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.790
I'll throw him a bone...

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:55.410
Mm-hmm, so he can fight in high spirits.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.420
Let's go, Yagi-chan!

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:01.670
We shall battle, Takamura-dono!

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.210
"D-Dono"?
